host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title The doc that described its neighbor, and the citation that can prove it
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Standfast on reds first, read the council rota row, condense REMEMBER, send the increment
think Standfast opened the lap. grep for OPEN in crux/REDS.md found nothing live -- every row through %133 carries a CLOSED twin -- so the ledger was clear.
think Found the real opening condition in the tree rather than the card: 103 files stood STAGED and uncommitted from the previous lap, with their session log written and never shipped. A lap that ends without a send leaves the next lap holding two rounds, so the first job was proving that increment green and sending it as its own signed round.
think Council rota, lap 167, row 167 mod 5 = 2 -- the Fire/Mars triad, cut and stop. Standfast names the stop itself, reds-first names where the hours go once the cord is pulled, and the three depths of removal name how deep a cut goes. The row fit the lap exactly: a fold is the gentlest depth, since a body lifted into one home destroys nothing.
think Ran tools/caravan_ladder_carry_witness.rish GREEN at carry 69,805 against a ceiling of 69,805, then the choir and the era suite, so the staged increment was proven on the tree it actually ran on before any of it shipped.
think Priced the next fold head with sh tools/fixtures/ladder_reach_visibility_scan.sh read_count -- declared=45 identical=43 folding=43 lines=14 reached=2 widens=0 stub=3 fall=462, the last zero-widening row on the board.
think Hashed all forty-five read_count bodies. Forty-three matched; caravan/confer.rye and caravan/revoke.rye differed by exactly two lines -- the omitted assert(suffix.len >= 1) and its invariant comment. The same pair diverged the same way under read_words last lap, so the shape was familiar rather than new.
think Read every read_count call site in both rungs before judging the omission. All five pass string literals -- ".offered", ".given", ".held" -- so the assert holds at every one and the omission is an accident rather than a contract, unlike revoke.rye's deliberate difference under read_words.
think Then read the harness itself around the insertion point, which is the part twelve previous lifts had skipped, and found the red: a twenty-four-line doc block beginning "Writes one note for a dependent" sat directly above pub fn read_words, and pub fn seat_note twenty lines below it carried no doc at all.
think Confirmed the mechanism rather than assuming it. The seat_note lift inserted its declaration BELOW read_words while placing its doc block ABOVE it. Zig binds a doc comment to the next declaration, so read_words -- which reads a word list into a bounded buffer -- was documented as writing a note, complete with the fold arithmetic of a family it has nothing to do with.
think Audited all one hundred and forty declarations in the harness for the same shape before repairing one, since a defect found once is a sample rather than a census. This misattachment is isolated; the other undocumented functions are private check delegators, a different and pre-existing pattern.
think Chose the guard by asking what the file already states about itself. Every fold's doc block carries the widening meter's own REACH_OK family=X citation, which is the block's own statement of what it documents -- so the check is a name against a name rather than a reading of prose, which is the only kind of prose check worth building.
think First draft of the scan read one citation of seven. The citation wraps where the prose wraps, so REACH_OK can close one line while family=X opens the next. Widened the match to take family= wherever it stands inside the block, and it read all seven.
obs REDS %134 booked and closed in the same lap. The block moved down to sit above pub fn seat_note, read_words kept its own one-line summary, and tools/fixtures/ladder_doc_attachment_scan.sh now refuses any block whose cited family differs from the pub fn beneath it.
obs Three legs prove on metal, and the third is the one that matters most. A misattached block is refused in the exact shape the red wore; a harness carrying no citation refuses rather than blessing its own blindness; and a correctly attached block is WELCOMED, because a gate that reds on valid input teaches a bench to route around it -- the Radiant pass playbook's own rule for blocking witnesses, applied to a scan.
obs The class this closes is one no witness on the ladder could ever have caught. Every Caravan witness proves behavior, and a doc comment has none -- so both wrong claims rode a signed commit through a hundred and eight green witnesses without a murmur. Prose about code is checkable only where the prose names something the code also names, and the family citation was already there.
obs The era roster grew from ten rungs to eleven, and every rung's own count claim moved with it. A first pass replaced them too coarsely and left the stub rung reading 11/11 beside the new one; caught by reading the roster back rather than by trusting the edit.
obs The residue is named rather than papered over: the guard binds only blocks carrying a family= citation, so a fold that stops writing the citation stops being seen. Every fold of this arc writes it, which is what makes the check worth its weight.
loom reds_134 harness_declarations=140 cited_blocks=7 docs_adrift_before=1 docs_adrift_after=0
loom caravan_choir witnesses=108 verdict=GREEN era_suite_rungs=11
loom caravan_carry carried=69805 ceiling=69805 bodies=18173 distinct=7971 families=703 modules=110
loom read_count_queue declared=45 identical=43 lines=14 reached=2 widens=0 stub=3 predicted_fall=462
file caravan/ladder_checks.rye the seat_note doc block moved down to the declaration it describes
file tools/fixtures/ladder_doc_attachment_scan.sh the new guard -- a fold's family citation checked against the pub fn beneath it
file tools/ladder_doc_attachment_witness.rish three legs on generated controls, both refusals and the welcome
file tools/glow_tend_era_suite.rish the roster grown to eleven rungs, every denominator moved with it
file crux/REDS.md row %134 booked and closed, headline and span re-derived by the monotone witness
recommend keep-going read_count at 462 over forty-three rungs is priced and clear -- confer.rye and revoke.rye regain the suffix invariant by folding, so the family lifts forty-five rather than forty-three
